From cf4a34c4e684b3e655684e0cf709e1045dfbe642 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:31:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AmgX: fixes of the review of the wrapper

- the resources of AmgX keep the handle of MPI_COMM_WORLD instead of a
  duplicate: their creation and destruction are no longer collective
  (AmgX duplicates the communicator itself)
- a hypre matrix on a communicator of one process is uploaded as a local
  matrix
- collective checks in SetOperator: each process owns rows, global
  number of rows in the range of int
- the solver can't be used after a failed setup; sizes of the vectors
  checked in Mult
- AmgXPCG refuses relative tolerances below the floors of the convergence
  criteria of AmgX (1e-12 in double precision, 1e-6 in single precision)
  and requires a relative tolerance in single precision
- verbose cycles: negative tolerance, so that the residual computed for
  the statistics can't stop the cycle
- copy of the solver deleted; MPI_Finalized checked before printing
- documentation: link order with a MFEM containing AmgX, destruction
  before MPI_Finalize, exit with a solver alive
- tests: verbosity, default options, small right hand side, failed setup,
  invalid sizes, tolerance floors, solver on the first process only,
  communicator of one process, processes in reverse order, process
  without rows, full reinitialisation in parallel, no visible GPU
